WEBVTT

00:00.860 --> 00:03.530
Previously on Final Space ...

00:03.570 --> 00:06.570
Gary and Avocato got their
butt cheeks in a hot fight.

00:06.600 --> 00:09.000
The Lord Commander is hot
on their trail. Oh, crap!

00:09.040 --> 00:11.740
Now our heroes have joined
forces to protect Mooncake

00:11.770 --> 00:14.480
and save Avocato's son,
Little Cato.

00:14.510 --> 00:17.010
What are they going to do?
Where are they going to hide?

00:17.050 --> 00:18.380
I have no idea.

00:18.410 --> 00:20.780
That's why we're watching
this episode, y'all!

00:23.620 --> 00:27.320
You have 7 minutes
of oxygen left, Gary.

00:27.360 --> 00:31.060
Phew. Look, it's Carl.
Carl, how's life?

00:31.090 --> 00:33.230
Carl is dead, Gary.

00:33.260 --> 00:35.000
Classic Carl.

00:35.030 --> 00:37.030
That bastard owes me 25 bucks.

00:37.070 --> 00:39.340
-Man: Mayday, mayday!
-Can you clean that up, HUE?

00:39.370 --> 00:40.670
HUE: I can try.

00:40.700 --> 00:42.540
There is quite a bit
of interference.

00:42.570 --> 00:44.510
-Man: We need help!
-Any idea who it is?

00:44.540 --> 00:47.340
HUE: No, Gary.
I'm afraid not.

00:47.380 --> 00:50.080
Well, maybe I can help these --

00:50.110 --> 00:52.750
Actually, I'll just
chill over here.

00:52.780 --> 01:02.060
♪♪

01:02.090 --> 01:11.270
♪♪

01:11.300 --> 01:20.780
♪♪

01:20.810 --> 01:28.280
[ Beatboxing ]

01:28.320 --> 01:30.950
For you!

01:30.990 --> 01:32.290
This will help.

01:32.320 --> 01:34.760
What is this? Who's there?

01:34.790 --> 01:41.460
♪♪

01:41.500 --> 01:46.100
Your father is a coward!

01:46.140 --> 01:48.340
My father will come for me,

01:48.370 --> 01:50.310
and he will kill you

01:50.340 --> 01:53.510
if I don't first.

01:53.540 --> 01:57.350
Yah! Ow.

02:00.020 --> 02:01.680
Quinn, do I look
any different?

02:01.720 --> 02:03.190
I should because
you're looking

02:03.220 --> 02:06.260
at the most wanted
man in the galaxy.

02:06.290 --> 02:08.190
Oh, look who it is.

02:08.220 --> 02:10.030
Avocato, come say hi to Quinn.

02:10.060 --> 02:11.090
No.

02:11.130 --> 02:12.330
He's a bit of a grouch,

02:12.360 --> 02:14.130
but his son has been kidnapped.

02:14.160 --> 02:15.530
Yeah. I know.

02:15.560 --> 02:18.000
Anyways, big development.
I have a robot arm.

02:18.030 --> 02:20.840
Look at this!
Oh, my god! How do I...

02:20.870 --> 02:24.010
Ahh! Ahh! Oh!

02:24.040 --> 02:26.940
I think that's all
I have for you today.

02:26.980 --> 02:28.840
Give me a call, Quinn.

02:28.880 --> 02:31.510
Oh, I almost forgot.
In four days, I'm a free man.

02:31.550 --> 02:32.720
What do you say when I turn...

02:32.750 --> 02:37.050
Proximity alert.
Proximity alert.

02:37.090 --> 02:38.850
Gary, we are taking fire

02:38.890 --> 02:41.890
from the Lord Commander's
heavy incinerators.

02:47.700 --> 02:50.170
Grab it firm.
What do we do, HUE?

02:50.200 --> 02:52.240
Calculating. I am detecting

02:52.270 --> 02:54.140
an incursion
in our proximity.

02:54.170 --> 02:56.000
-A what?
-A temporal worm, Gary.

02:56.040 --> 02:57.540
It's your only option.

02:57.570 --> 02:59.710
A temporal worm could send us
backwards or forwards

02:59.740 --> 03:01.510
thousands of years
in time, Gary.

03:01.540 --> 03:03.880
Are you sure that's
the only choice we have?

03:03.910 --> 03:05.680
Feed us to it!

03:05.710 --> 03:12.320
♪♪

03:12.360 --> 03:17.230
[ Alarm blaring ]

03:17.260 --> 03:20.330
Whoa!

03:20.360 --> 03:22.060
Aah!

03:22.100 --> 03:26.940
Mm, pressed hams.

03:31.240 --> 03:32.540
That was wondrous!

03:32.580 --> 03:34.410
How about covering up
that dick situation

03:34.440 --> 03:36.040
you've got going there?
Jeez.

03:36.080 --> 03:37.280
In good time.

03:37.310 --> 03:40.080
Speaking of which,
when are we?

03:40.120 --> 03:41.420
Happy?

03:41.450 --> 03:42.520
Gary, we have jumped

03:42.550 --> 03:44.620
four days into the future.

03:44.650 --> 03:46.920
Wait. What? That means my last
four days of jail are up.

03:46.960 --> 03:50.790
Right, HUE? Open sesame!
Unlock my bounty!

03:50.830 --> 03:52.930
Clause nine
of your imprisonment

03:52.960 --> 03:55.700
stipulates that all
time-related disruptions

03:55.730 --> 03:57.900
have zero effect
on your sentence.

03:57.930 --> 04:00.040
What? So no chocolate
treasure coins?

04:00.070 --> 04:02.270
Are you referring
to cookies, Gary?

04:02.310 --> 04:04.410
-Yes!
-Oh, then no.

04:04.440 --> 04:07.540
This is a load, HUE, a load!

04:07.580 --> 04:09.910
Listen, Gary.
We're marked targets,

04:09.950 --> 04:11.950
and no matter what
hole we hide in,

04:11.980 --> 04:14.380
the Lord Commander will
find us in our hole

04:14.420 --> 04:16.720
and take Mooncake
from that hole.

04:16.750 --> 04:18.450
I know that's
a whole lot of holes,

04:18.490 --> 04:20.320
but we're in a whole
lot of trouble.

04:20.360 --> 04:23.990
-HUE?
-Avocato is correct.

04:24.030 --> 04:26.130
We need to hide him
until we figure things out.

04:26.160 --> 04:28.830
Look. I've heard of a place
that safeguards fugitives.

04:28.860 --> 04:33.470
The closest one is on Yarno.
No one will find him there.

04:33.500 --> 04:36.000
HUE, spool up the engines.

04:36.040 --> 04:38.140
We're going to Yarno.

04:38.170 --> 04:44.750
♪♪

04:44.780 --> 04:48.820
Helper Hula, I've always
respected the Order of the 12

04:48.850 --> 04:51.320
being the eyes
of the universe.

04:51.350 --> 04:56.190
Where is E 35-1?

04:56.220 --> 04:59.630
Ah! You're dying!

04:59.660 --> 05:02.630
Dying? Really, genius?
I know I'm dying!

05:02.670 --> 05:05.830
Every time
you use your light,

05:05.870 --> 05:08.600
you quicken your own death.

05:08.640 --> 05:12.010
That's why I need Mooncake,

05:12.040 --> 05:14.510
or whatever that idiot
calls him.

05:14.540 --> 05:17.950
I need him to live.
Tell me where he is.

05:17.980 --> 05:20.680
Patience.

05:20.720 --> 05:23.290
That wasn't very helpful.

05:23.320 --> 05:31.230
♪♪

05:31.260 --> 05:33.200
Ugh!

05:33.230 --> 05:36.400
[ Coughing ]

05:38.730 --> 05:41.470
You will find him for me,

05:41.500 --> 05:45.010
or next time I finish the job.

05:48.510 --> 05:51.380
[ Soft roar of engine ]

05:57.290 --> 06:02.490
Gworplo! I'm Zargon Tukalishi,
and welcome to Yarn--

06:02.530 --> 06:07.700
[ Screaming nonsense ]

06:07.730 --> 06:09.900
Looks like they've made
some changes around here.

06:09.930 --> 06:11.700
You don't say, because
the Deathcropolis

06:11.730 --> 06:13.500
just sounded like
a lovely church picnic.

06:13.540 --> 06:15.670
[ Whimpering ]
Don't worry, Mooncake.

06:15.700 --> 06:17.170
We got this.

06:17.210 --> 06:21.010
Moonobumps, homemade moonobumps.

06:21.040 --> 06:24.850
Oh, sweet! They're just handing
out free candy!

06:24.880 --> 06:28.680
Wow. Whoa.

06:28.720 --> 06:30.620
Oh, oh,

06:30.650 --> 06:34.120
he has
a Popsicle now!

06:34.160 --> 06:36.530
Ahh!

06:36.560 --> 06:38.860
[ Gasping ]

06:38.890 --> 06:40.260
I feel so replenished.

06:40.300 --> 06:43.600
Oh, wow. Oh!
Just what is this?

06:43.630 --> 06:46.470
There's a dart sticking
out of my chesticles!

06:46.500 --> 06:49.270
Can you not take crap
from weird alien skeevoids?

06:49.300 --> 06:53.540
Noted, "Do not take
crap from skeevoids."

06:53.580 --> 06:55.210
Ugh.
Ahh!

06:55.240 --> 06:57.380
Ahh!
[ Laughing ]

06:57.410 --> 07:00.950
♪♪

07:00.980 --> 07:02.620
There's a quantum
gravitational disturbance

07:02.650 --> 07:04.550
emanating two parsecs
from Jupiter.

07:04.590 --> 07:06.890
If my math is right,
all our lives might depend --

07:06.920 --> 07:10.330
Quinn, it's Triborn.
Don't worry. I'm at your place.

07:10.360 --> 07:13.730
Everything is okay,
but super bad news.

07:13.760 --> 07:15.400
You're not going to like it.

07:15.430 --> 07:17.230
In fact, I don't know
what happened to all the like.

07:17.270 --> 07:18.630
Where did all the like go?

07:18.670 --> 07:21.240
Tell me, already!
I will tell you, already.

07:21.270 --> 07:24.110
Superior Stone dispatched
an Imperium cruiser

07:24.140 --> 07:25.810
yesterday to apprehend you

07:25.840 --> 07:30.010
because you kind of broke
a lot of laws, like 47 laws.

07:30.050 --> 07:31.350
Why didn't you tell me sooner?

07:31.380 --> 07:32.920
Why didn't I tell you sooner?

07:32.950 --> 07:34.420
That is the question, isn't it?

07:34.450 --> 07:36.020
The answer, I've been busy.

07:36.050 --> 07:37.420
Are you touching my stuff?

07:37.450 --> 07:39.090
Why would I be
touching your stuff.

07:39.120 --> 07:40.790
It makes me look
so dreamy and beautiful.

07:40.820 --> 07:42.930
I would never be touching
your beautiful stuff.

07:42.960 --> 07:47.130
Quinn, an Imperium cruiser
is closing in on your position.

07:50.130 --> 07:52.030
-This is the place, Gary.
-This is the place?

07:52.070 --> 07:53.770
This, right here, is the place?

07:53.800 --> 07:56.640
I'm not going down there.

07:56.670 --> 07:58.940
Welcome, friends,
to the Order of 12

07:58.970 --> 08:00.780
Yarno chapter --
a representative

08:00.810 --> 08:02.140
will meet you shortly.

08:02.180 --> 08:03.780
How can I --
Jeez!

08:03.810 --> 08:06.280
...help?

08:06.310 --> 08:08.020
You got me.
Are you a helper?

08:08.050 --> 08:09.120
Oh, no.

08:09.150 --> 08:12.120
I assist the helpers.

08:12.150 --> 08:14.160
[ Chuckling ]

08:14.190 --> 08:16.190
So you're a helper-helper?

08:16.220 --> 08:19.630
I will tell him
you have...

08:19.660 --> 08:22.060
arrived.

08:22.100 --> 08:24.130
Guy straight up ghosted
through that wall.

08:24.170 --> 08:25.500
Live with it.
I can't.

08:25.530 --> 08:29.840
The guy just ghosted
through that wall, yo.

08:29.870 --> 08:31.640
Ahh!
How can I help?

08:31.670 --> 08:34.540
We love to help.
Thanks.

08:34.580 --> 08:37.050
Well, we need to find a safe
place for my little buddy.

08:37.080 --> 08:41.080
Sorry.
We're at capacity.

08:41.120 --> 08:44.150
[ Whimpers ]
Oh!

08:44.190 --> 08:47.060
But we could always
squeeze in one more.

08:47.090 --> 08:50.830
Such a precious specimen.

08:50.860 --> 08:52.230
Mm-hmm, mm-hmm.

08:52.260 --> 08:55.100
C-can you say that just
a little less creepy-like?

08:56.700 --> 08:58.770
Okay. I guess not.

08:58.800 --> 09:00.500
Mooncake.
Chocatey?

09:00.540 --> 09:04.110
No one's saying
goodbye, here. Okay?

09:04.140 --> 09:05.540
I'll be back as soon as I can.

09:05.570 --> 09:09.010
It's only temporary.
I promise.

09:09.040 --> 09:11.680
Chocatey pah.

09:11.710 --> 09:14.180
[ Squeaking ]
Gary, he'll be fine.

09:14.220 --> 09:15.950
He can take care of himself.

09:15.980 --> 09:19.350
♪♪

09:19.390 --> 09:22.060
By the way, I never got
your name, mister...

09:22.090 --> 09:24.190
Stevil.
Whoa!

09:24.230 --> 09:25.590
Whoa, whoa, whoa,
whoa, whoa. Pump the breaks.

09:25.630 --> 09:28.030
Okay. The freaking guy has evil
in his name.

09:28.060 --> 09:31.200
I'm not handing Mooncake over
to a guy freaking named Stevil!

09:31.230 --> 09:32.530
Stevil is a bit alarming.

09:32.570 --> 09:35.440
It is a bit alarming!
We only want to help!

09:35.470 --> 09:36.910
Avocato, let's find
another place.

09:36.940 --> 09:38.740
Let's go.
STOP!

09:38.770 --> 09:40.210
Okay.

09:40.240 --> 09:43.310
This is full-blown banshee
screech, alarming!

09:47.080 --> 09:50.090
Mooncake!
Sleep.

09:52.520 --> 09:56.490
Alert High Helper Hula
we have been most helpful.

09:56.520 --> 10:04.570
♪♪

10:04.600 --> 10:08.300
Stevil lived right up
to the evil in his name!

10:08.340 --> 10:11.340
Look! We made it to the super
safe oblivion amusement park

10:11.370 --> 10:13.140
of never-ending
unsafe stairs!

10:13.180 --> 10:15.140
What fun! Thanks, Avocato.

10:15.180 --> 10:16.580
It's a Lazarus trap.

10:16.610 --> 10:18.610
Only master trap-makers
can make these,

10:18.650 --> 10:20.150
and people who
really like stairs.

10:20.180 --> 10:21.950
At least we're not
sinking into, like,

10:21.980 --> 10:23.620
a lake of lava or something.

10:26.020 --> 10:29.420
Listen to me. Anything we think
of becomes reality. Okay?

10:29.460 --> 10:32.360
Right. Okay. So we've
got to think positive.

10:32.390 --> 10:34.360
Ooh, ooh! Cookies!

10:34.400 --> 10:36.360
No!
Hey!

10:36.400 --> 10:38.470
Eat me! I'm delicious!
I'm a cookie!

10:38.500 --> 10:40.270
What? It's not like
I'm imagining

10:40.300 --> 10:41.600
murderous killing confections?

10:41.640 --> 10:45.110
I'm going to kill you.
[ Both scream ]

10:45.140 --> 10:49.280
Everybody is super excited

10:49.310 --> 10:54.120
about today's sacrifices
at the Deathcropolis.

10:54.150 --> 10:57.050
Ooh!

10:57.090 --> 11:00.060
But you're not being sacrificed.

11:00.090 --> 11:03.230
The Lord Commander needs you.

11:03.260 --> 11:04.630
What is he doing?

11:04.660 --> 11:06.290
Chocatey pah!

11:06.330 --> 11:13.300
♪♪

11:13.340 --> 11:15.800
[ Cheering ]

11:15.840 --> 11:24.750
♪♪

11:28.420 --> 11:31.050
Quinn Airgon, we have
orders to arrest you

11:31.090 --> 11:32.690
for aerial grand theft.

11:32.720 --> 11:34.520
-Chuck?
-Yes. This is Chuck.

11:34.560 --> 11:37.690
Now, please surrender,
and this all goes away.

11:37.730 --> 11:40.030
Listen, jerk nuts.
No.

11:40.060 --> 11:42.060
Did she just call me jerk nuts?

11:42.100 --> 11:44.730
Oh. Okay, yeah. Yeah.

11:44.770 --> 11:46.370
I think you are under arrest.

11:46.400 --> 11:48.700
Hey! Douche canoe,
not happening.

11:48.740 --> 11:51.710
God. You said,
"Douche canoe."

11:51.740 --> 11:53.410
All right. Listen, Quinn.

11:53.440 --> 11:54.840
No. You listen.

11:54.880 --> 11:56.240
I'm trying to save
the world, here.

11:56.280 --> 11:58.250
So you're going to turn
your vessel around

11:58.280 --> 11:59.680
and forget you ever saw me.

11:59.710 --> 12:03.590
Dude, are you crying?
No. No, I'm not crying.

12:03.620 --> 12:07.190
It's space pollen.

12:07.220 --> 12:09.060
[ Engines powering down ]

12:09.090 --> 12:12.830
Ah, ah, ah!
Didn't say the magic word!

12:16.160 --> 12:20.440
Aaah! Why am I the only one
covered in cookies?

12:20.470 --> 12:21.940
You have no cookies!

12:21.970 --> 12:23.940
Gary, de-think the cookies!

12:23.970 --> 12:26.310
Not sure that's possible.
I'm a very creative guy.

12:26.340 --> 12:29.380
Like, wouldn't it be cool
if they had, like, laser eyes?

12:29.410 --> 12:30.450
Aah! Run!

12:30.480 --> 12:33.280
Oh, my God!
Think of something else.

12:33.320 --> 12:35.950
Anything else!
-What, like tridents?

12:35.980 --> 12:36.950
-No! No!
-Yeah! Yes!

12:36.990 --> 12:39.550
No! Not like tridents!

12:39.590 --> 12:41.120
I'm thinking about
little trident-wielding

12:41.160 --> 12:43.630
laser-shooting death cookies!

12:43.660 --> 12:45.290
I'm thinking of nothing,
nothing, nothing.

12:45.330 --> 12:47.230
Oh! Whoa! Oh!
Oh, my gosh.

12:47.260 --> 12:51.130
-I'm going to eat your eyes out.
-And pee in your sockets!

12:51.170 --> 12:54.140
You're never going
to leave this place.

12:54.170 --> 12:56.600
Why is that one cookie
lone-wolfing it across the edge?

12:56.640 --> 12:59.470
Oh! He's leaping! Whoa!
He's like an angel!

12:59.510 --> 13:01.910
Oh, my God --
I'm going to kill you.

13:01.940 --> 13:03.750
It's stabbing my eyes!

13:03.780 --> 13:06.180
Ahh!

13:06.210 --> 13:08.920
Ohh.

13:08.950 --> 13:13.360
[ Roaring ]

13:13.390 --> 13:15.990
Chocatey pah!

13:16.020 --> 13:17.990
[ Cheering ]

13:18.030 --> 13:21.830
To the ones who live
for the ones who die!

13:21.860 --> 13:25.770
♪♪

13:25.800 --> 13:29.340
It's not fair.
I've been good.

13:29.370 --> 13:31.270
I help people.

13:31.310 --> 13:35.640
I've been patient,
unbelievably patient!

13:35.680 --> 13:37.010
Oh, Lord Commander!

13:37.050 --> 13:39.010
I brought your medicine, sir!

13:39.050 --> 13:41.150
I put a little biscuit
on the side,

13:41.180 --> 13:45.020
just for you,
my special little prince.

13:45.050 --> 13:47.690
What is this?
Ugh! Gah!

13:47.720 --> 13:51.960
I like the much littler
kind of biscuits.

13:51.990 --> 13:55.030
I have told you this, Eric.

13:55.060 --> 13:57.370
I told you this!

13:57.400 --> 14:00.240
We have been most helpful.

14:00.270 --> 14:03.040
We have found Mooncake.

14:03.070 --> 14:05.710
My patience paid off.

14:05.740 --> 14:08.680
[ Choking ]

14:08.710 --> 14:11.050
[ Blasting ]

14:11.080 --> 14:19.050
♪♪

14:19.090 --> 14:20.760
The more you kill,

14:20.790 --> 14:25.360
the more the Twelve Titans
beyond rejoice.

14:28.400 --> 14:30.230
Ahh!

14:30.270 --> 14:32.430
Gary, we need to wake up.
Close your eyes.

14:32.470 --> 14:34.370
You want me to wake up
by closing my eyes?

14:34.400 --> 14:37.240
That doesn't make any sense!
Nothing makes any sense in here!

14:37.270 --> 14:38.840
All right. Good point.

14:38.870 --> 14:40.710
Okay. I'm closing my eyes.

14:40.740 --> 14:43.180
It's not working.

14:43.210 --> 14:46.080
-Hi, Gary.
-Quinn?

14:46.110 --> 14:48.220
It's been a long time.

14:48.250 --> 14:50.590
Come here. I missed you.

14:50.620 --> 14:53.620
Is it really you?

14:53.660 --> 14:55.260
Closer.

14:55.290 --> 14:57.790
Gary...
Get off me!

14:57.830 --> 14:59.090
It's part of the trap.

14:59.130 --> 15:01.630
Gary, don't listen to him.

15:01.660 --> 15:04.870
You need to trust me.
She isn't real.

15:04.900 --> 15:07.100
Are we going home, dad?

15:10.410 --> 15:13.610
Trust me, buddy.
We both need to wake up.

15:13.640 --> 15:16.910
♪♪

15:16.950 --> 15:19.610
I don't want to wake up.

15:19.650 --> 15:22.280
Then you're really not
going to want this.

15:27.320 --> 15:29.790
We're out! I saved us.

15:29.820 --> 15:32.390
No, I saved you.
And I, you.

15:32.430 --> 15:33.960
No, you didn't.
But I did.

15:34.000 --> 15:36.130
You almost got us killed, Gary.

15:36.160 --> 15:38.130
Then we're even.

15:38.170 --> 15:39.330
We've got to find Mooncake!

15:39.370 --> 15:40.770
Gary, I told you Mooncake

15:40.800 --> 15:41.900
is going to be okay.

15:41.940 --> 15:43.410
He's a super weapon.
Wrong!

15:43.440 --> 15:45.570
Little green ball friend
is a harmless gumball of love!

15:45.610 --> 15:47.980
HUE, you there?
Where have you been, Gary?

15:48.010 --> 15:50.480
It would sound too insane
to even explain.

15:50.510 --> 15:52.150
Can you lock into
Mooncake's location?

15:52.180 --> 15:54.750
Ugh!
Uh, Gary?

15:54.780 --> 15:57.150
Little buddy.

15:57.190 --> 16:00.590
The final sacrifice awaits.

16:00.620 --> 16:06.790
♪♪

16:06.830 --> 16:08.860
[ Whimpers ]

16:08.900 --> 16:13.000
Crowd [chanting]: Kill! Kill!
Kill! Kill!

16:13.040 --> 16:22.040
♪♪

16:22.080 --> 16:24.280
Hello, Mooncake.

16:24.310 --> 16:27.780
I have been looking
all over for you.

16:27.820 --> 16:30.720
♪♪

16:30.750 --> 16:33.360
Don't be shy.

16:33.390 --> 16:38.530
Come in and say hello.

16:38.560 --> 16:41.230
Ahh!

16:43.070 --> 16:46.000
How did I become so weak?

16:46.030 --> 16:49.200
-Mooncake!
-Doot, doot, doot, doot!

16:49.240 --> 16:50.540
Chocatey!
Oh!

16:50.570 --> 16:54.010
-Gary!
-It's over, The Gary.

16:54.040 --> 16:55.880
"Gary."
It's just "Gary."

16:55.910 --> 16:57.210
What is your deal, dude?

16:57.250 --> 16:59.080
Why won't you just
leave us alone?

16:59.110 --> 17:01.720
You have no idea, do you?

17:01.750 --> 17:04.220
Mooncake is the key.

17:04.250 --> 17:07.220
That being can unlock

17:07.260 --> 17:11.490
Final Space.

17:11.530 --> 17:14.100
What the mother-loving crap
is Final Space?

17:14.130 --> 17:16.100
That's my business.

17:16.130 --> 17:18.670
Should we play a game, Gary?

17:18.700 --> 17:21.900
I love games.
I always win.

17:21.940 --> 17:29.280
♪♪

17:29.310 --> 17:32.080
You know what I want,
and I --

17:32.110 --> 17:34.550
Ya!

17:34.580 --> 17:38.120
Oh, my gosh!

17:38.150 --> 17:40.720
[ Parts crashing ]

17:40.760 --> 17:45.260
Sweet Grandor's glove! You are a
planet-destroying super weapon!

17:45.290 --> 17:47.360
Chocatey!
Whoa! Yes!

17:47.400 --> 17:49.200
That's so freaking tight!

17:49.230 --> 17:52.070
That's not how we play the game!

17:52.100 --> 17:53.440
How about this game?

17:53.470 --> 17:56.140
Ah, you missed.
Freak.

17:56.170 --> 17:57.940
Shoot for the locks!

17:57.970 --> 18:04.380
♪♪

18:04.410 --> 18:07.250
Gary, look out!
Ugh!

18:07.280 --> 18:08.750
Ah! Ugh.

18:08.780 --> 18:14.990
♪♪

18:15.020 --> 18:17.090
I'm going to save you, Gary!

18:17.130 --> 18:18.930
I'm saving you!

18:18.960 --> 18:20.230
I'm here to save you, Gary!

18:20.260 --> 18:22.330
The day is saved.

18:22.360 --> 18:24.400
Freaking KVN!
I hate you so much!

18:24.430 --> 18:26.130
I truly can't wait
for the day you die!

18:26.170 --> 18:27.940
Oh, my gosh. No one will be sad.

18:27.970 --> 18:30.140
There will only be happiness!

18:30.170 --> 18:34.810
[ KVN laughing ]

18:34.840 --> 18:36.480
Hey, Gary!

18:36.510 --> 18:38.850
Don't even. Just don't even.

18:38.880 --> 18:40.820
KVN has saved everything.

18:40.850 --> 18:42.150
[ Beeping ]

18:42.180 --> 18:43.320
[ Crunch ]

18:43.350 --> 18:48.620
♪♪

18:51.390 --> 18:52.930
The gravitational disturbance,
it's massive

18:52.960 --> 18:55.530
and growing -- a lot...

18:55.560 --> 18:56.930
a lot, a lot.

18:56.960 --> 18:58.370
That's what I've been
trying to tell you.

18:58.400 --> 19:01.170
Probe failure imminent.
Probe failure imminent.

19:01.200 --> 19:05.470
We need to get out
of here right now.

19:05.510 --> 19:08.380
Oh, God!
Engage rear thrusters!

19:08.410 --> 19:10.550
Ahh! Ah!

19:10.580 --> 19:12.880
[ Grunting ]

19:12.910 --> 19:15.620
I am not a douche canoe!

19:15.650 --> 19:17.690
Ahh!

19:17.720 --> 19:20.290
♪♪

19:20.320 --> 19:21.620
Ahh!

19:21.660 --> 19:30.130
♪♪

19:30.160 --> 19:38.240
♪♪

19:38.270 --> 19:40.680
Mayday, mayday!
This is Quinn Airgon.

19:40.710 --> 19:43.250
Can someone hear me?
Help me!

19:45.710 --> 19:47.920
I've processed your scan
of all prisoner

19:47.950 --> 19:50.180
transfers out of
Tera Con Prime.

19:50.220 --> 19:53.090
There is no match
for Little Cato.

19:53.120 --> 19:58.560
♪♪

19:58.590 --> 20:03.570
♪♪

20:03.600 --> 20:05.770
Mooncake?

20:05.800 --> 20:07.440
What's wrong, bud?

20:07.470 --> 20:08.840
Mm.

20:08.870 --> 20:11.210
I get it.

20:11.240 --> 20:14.440
So you shoot a murder beam
out of your face hole.

20:14.480 --> 20:17.850
So what? I mean, it happens
to the best of us.

20:17.880 --> 20:20.180
I mean, just the other day
I had a burrito,

20:20.210 --> 20:22.620
and you should have saw
the freaking murder beam

20:22.650 --> 20:23.950
that came out of my ba--

20:23.990 --> 20:25.450
And, you know,
it's actually pretty sweet,

20:25.490 --> 20:27.120
if you think about it.

20:27.150 --> 20:29.220
I mean, I just want you to know
that that doesn't change

20:29.260 --> 20:31.630
anything between you
and this guy.

20:31.660 --> 20:32.930
[Gasps]
Me?

20:32.960 --> 20:34.460
Not you!
Chocatey!

20:37.400 --> 20:38.630
Him.

20:38.670 --> 20:39.970
It doesn't make you the bad guy.

20:40.000 --> 20:41.300
It really doesn't.
I mean, it makes the scum

20:41.340 --> 20:44.140
who want to use you
as the weapon the bad guy.

20:44.170 --> 20:46.370
Look, you're a good guy
to the max core.

20:46.410 --> 20:47.640
Ohh!

20:47.680 --> 20:49.380
I'm never going
to let you go again.

20:49.410 --> 20:52.310
I now know the only one
I can trust with you

20:52.350 --> 20:54.620
is my own awesomeness.

20:54.650 --> 20:56.820
Mm!
[ Laughs ]

20:56.850 --> 20:58.550
I'm starting to like these.

20:58.590 --> 20:59.990
Mm.

21:00.020 --> 21:02.820
Gary, I am receiving
a mayday call.

21:02.860 --> 21:04.830
Mayday, mayday!
This is Quinn Airgon!

21:04.860 --> 21:07.500
Can someone hear me? Help me!

21:07.530 --> 21:10.600
Oh, my crap. It's Quinn.

21:10.630 --> 21:13.770
♪♪

21:13.800 --> 21:16.400
[ Groaning, coughing ]

21:16.440 --> 21:19.670
[ Grumbles ]

21:19.710 --> 21:29.320
♪♪
